summary:
  The stop hands kill the whole pid file, which now holds three numbers.

history:
  The pid file names the writer's owner since the startup sweep needed it
  ("writer shell host"). Read whole, as it was when it held one number, it
  is a single word kill cannot use: nothing is stopped, and every station
  change leaves the previous writer copying its stream.

target:
  package/contents/ui/TimeshiftLogic.js

find:
      return ": TS_STOP; " + srv + "[ -f " + q(pidPath) + " ] && read -r p _ < " + q(pidPath)

replace:
      return ": TS_STOP; " + srv + "[ -f " + q(pidPath) + " ] && p=$(cat " + q(pidPath) + ")"

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_timeshiftlogic.qml::test_the_stop_kills_the_first_field_of_the_pid_file.
  Line-neutral.
